1:1 COMMENT "# os_spawn.z -- run a child process and read back its exit code."
1:65 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "#"
2:2 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# `os.spawn` runs `argv[0]` (resolved via PATH) as a child with stdin from the"
3:79 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# null device and stdout/stderr redirected to the given paths; it returns the"
4:78 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# child's exit status. The child is this program run again with the code to"
5:76 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# end with, so the example needs nothing else installed, on any system."
6:72 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "# Letting main return normally (no os.exit) runs the argv destructors, so the"
7:78 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "# leak gate stays clean; the children end with os.exit, which skips them."
8:74 EOL "\n"
9:1 EOL "\n"
